Finding: {"title":"Draft weekStart/date-range fallbacks use UTC calendar day, not the location's timezone","severity":"LOW","area":"Timezone correctness","files":["src/server/routes/routes-ai-schedule.ts"],"detail":"POST /drafts (weekStart default, line 425), POST /drafts/instructor-create (weekStart default, line 1152), and existing-events/generate date-range iteration (lines 355-360, 2280-2286) all derive 'today' or date-range boundaries via `new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0]` or `new Date(`${d}T00:00:00`)` — UTC-anchored — while the rest of the AI-schedule domain (utcToLocalHour/localHourToUtcDate, the sandbox UI's dateToStr) is explicitly location-timezone-aware. For a location like America/Phoenix (UTC-7), a request between midnight UTC and 7am UTC (5pm-midnight local the prior day) computes 'today' one calendar day ahead of the location's actual local date.","impact":"Draft names/labels or default week-start values can be off by one day for schools west of UTC during evening hours; low impact since these are mostly fallback/display fields (draft events themselves carry an explicit `date` from the client), but it's the same class of bug the codebase has fixed elsewhere via the utcToLocalHour helpers.","recommendation":"Route these fallbacks through the location's timezone (already loaded via locationRepository.findByIdMinimal in the same request in most cases) instead of raw UTC `Date`/`toISOString()`.","confidence":"medium"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

